[{"w":"a","s":"abhāva-bheda-aprādhānya-īṣat-sādṛśya-virodhārtheṣu","e":"(i) absence, e.g ananta (“endless”) (ii) difference, e.g asat (“not good”) (iii) inferiority, e.g ayajña (“a lousy sacrifice”) (iv) diminutiveness, e.g anudara (“having a small belly, thin”) (v) similarity, e.g abrāhmaṇa (“like a brāhmaṇa”) (vi) oppositeness, e.g asita (“opposite to white, black”)"},{"w":"akasmāt","s":"akāraṇāt, haṭhāt","e":"accidentally, causelessly; suddenly"},{"w":"agratas","s":"prathame, sammukhe","e":"first, in front of"},{"w":"aghos","s":"sambodhane","e":"O sinful one"},{"w":"aṅga","s":"sambodhane","e":"O dear one"},{"w":"acirāt","s":"śīghram","e":"quickly"},{"w":"añjasā","s":"śīghram, satyam","e":"quickly; truly"},{"w":"aṭṭaṭṭa","s":"ucca-śabde","e":"loudly"},{"w":"atas","s":"ata eva","e":"therefore"},{"w":"ati","s":"adhikam","e":"very, beyond"},{"w":"atīva","s":"atiśayam, adhikam","e":"extremely; beyond"},{"w":"atra","s":"asmin","e":"in this, here"},{"w":"atha","s":"maṅgalānantarārambha-praśna-kārtsnyārtheṣu","e":"(i) auspiciousness, e.g atha yogānuśāsanam (ii) contiguousness, e.g imaṁ dīkṣaya, atha enaṁ pāṭhaya (“initiate this person. (then) Teach him”) (iii) beginning, e.g atha viṣṇupada-prakaraṇam (“now we begin the section on viṣṇupadas”) (iv) questioning, e.g atha śaknoṣi bhoktum (“are you able to eat?”), but usually with another interrogative: athātra- bhavatī katham ittham-bhūtā (“why is Her Honour like this?”) (v) entirety, e.g atha dharmaṁ vyākhyāsyāmaḥ (“we shall explain dharma in its entirety”)"},{"w":"atha kim","s":"svī-kāre","e":"yes"},{"w":"atho","s":"maṅgalānantarārambha-praśna-kārtsnyārtheṣu","e":"same as atha"},{"w":"addhā","s":"satyam, yathārtham","e":"truly; properly"},{"w":"adya","s":"adya, idānīm","e":"today, now"},{"w":"adharāt","s":"nīcārthe","e":"down, under, below"},{"w":"adhareṇa","s":"nīcārthe","e":"down, under, below"},{"w":"adhas","s":"nīcārthe","e":"down, under, below"},{"w":"adhastāt","s":"nīcārthe","e":"down, under, below"},{"w":"adhunā","s":"idānīm","e":"now"},{"w":"anu","s":"paścāt, lakṣī-kṛtya","e":"after; towards, in regard to, according to"},{"w":"anupadam Some of the meanings of the avyayas listed here are left out. For more thorough definitions, consult Amara-koṣa. The a mentioned here is just the paryudāsa variety of na[ñ] described in Amṛta. The paryudāsa na[ñ] is used in the six senses mentioned here and it always becomes a or an, in accordance with naño ’-rāma-śeṣaḥ, sarveśvare tu nuṭ ca samāse (788), because it is always used in samāsa. The prasajya-pratiṣedha variety of na[ñ], however, is always used as a separate word in the sentence and only conveys the sense of negation (niṣedha). Thus it is mentioned separately in this list of avyayas. For further details regarding na[ñ], see Amṛta. This is the opening phrase to Patañjali’s Yoga-sūtras. The very mention of the word atha invokes auspiciousness because the word originally emanated from the throat of Brahmā as is apparent from the following verse: oṁkāraś cātha-śabdaś ca, dvāv etau brahmaṇaḥ purā, kaṇṭhaṁ bhittvā viniryātau, tena māṅgalikāv ubhau (“in the beginning, the syllable om and the word atha emerged by passing through the throat of Brahmā, thus they are both auspicious”). Usually atha is simultaneously used in the sense of beginning and auspiciousness. antatas","s":"tad-anantaram śeṣārthe, nyūnārthe finally; in the lowest way","e":"after that, then"},{"w":"antar","s":"madhye, śeṣe, antaḥkaraṇe ca","e":"between, among, within; remainder, end; the heart, mind, soul"},{"w":"antarā","s":"vyatirekeṇa, madhye","e":"without, except; between, among"},{"w":"antareṇa","s":"vinā","e":"without, except"},{"w":"anyat","s":"anya-prakāraḥ","e":"besides, on the other way"},{"w":"anyataredyus","s":"dvayor madhye eka-dine","e":"on either of two days"},{"w":"anyatas","s":"anyatra, anya-prakāreṇa","e":"elsewhere; otherwise"},{"w":"anyatra","s":"anya-sthāne, anya-viṣaye","e":"elsewhere; on the other hand"},{"w":"anyathā","s":"anyena prakāreṇa","e":"otherwise"},{"w":"anyadā","s":"anyasmin samaye","e":"at another time"},{"w":"anyedyus","s":"apara-dine","e":"on the other day, on the following day"},{"w":"aparedyus","s":"apara-dine","e":"on the other day, on the following day"},{"w":"abhi","s":"prati","e":"towards"},{"w":"abhitas","s":"sarvasyāṁ diśi, samīpe","e":"all around, in every direction; near"},{"w":"amā","s":"saha, candra-kalāyām","e":"with; one sixteenth part of the moon"},{"w":"amutra","s":"para-loke","e":"in the other world"},{"w":"ayi","s":"komala-sambodhane, praśne ca","e":"vocative of tender calling; a particle of kind inquiry"},{"w":"aye","s":"sambodhane smaraṇe ca","e":"vocative; particle of remembrance"},{"w":"are","s":"nīca-sambodhane","e":"vocative for an inferior person"},{"w":"are re","s":"nīca-sambodhane","e":"vocative for an inferior person"},{"w":"arvāk","s":"pūrve, paścāt, vakrārthe ca","e":"before; after; turned towards"},{"w":"arvāc","s":"pūrve, paścāt, vakrārthe ca","e":"before; after; turned towards"},{"w":"alam","s":"vyartha-samarthayoḥ","e":"enough of, no need of, e.g alaṁ lakṣa-lābhaiḥ (“Thousands and thousands of other benedictions are of no use to me”); sufficient, able to, e.g alaṁ bhoktum (“able to eat”)"},{"w":"avaśyam","s":"niścaye","e":"certainly"},{"w":"asi","s":"tvam-arthe","e":"you"},{"w":"astam","s":"adarśane, nāśe","e":"disappearance; destruction"},{"w":"asti","s":"bhavaty-arthe, tiṣṭhaty-arthe ca","e":"existent; present"},{"w":"astu","s":"bhavatu","e":"so be it"},{"w":"asmi","s":"aham-arthe","e":"I"},{"w":"ahaha","s":"khede, āścarye ca","e":"interjection of lamentation or wonder"},{"w":"ahahā","s":"khede, āścarye ca","e":"interjection of lamentation or wonder"},{"w":"ahe","s":"sambodhane","e":"vocative of reproach or rejection"},{"w":"aho","s":"āścarye","e":"interjection of wonder, e.g aho gītasya mādhuryam (“Oh, the sweetness of the song!”, or “What a sweet song!”)"},{"w":"aho bata","s":"kāruṇye","e":"interjection of compassion, translatable as “alas”"},{"w":"ahnāya","s":"śīghram, tat-kṣaṇāt","e":"quickly; instantly"},{"w":"ā              smaraṇe, paryantārthe ca","s":"","e":"particle of remembrance; or in the sense of limit"},{"w":"ām","s":"smaraṇe, svī-kāre ca","e":"particle of remembrance; yes"},{"w":"āḥ","s":"viraktau pīḍāyāṁ ca","e":"interjection of disaffection or pain"},{"w":"ārāt","s":"dūre, samīpe ca","e":"far; near"},{"w":"āvis","s":"prakāśe","e":"manifestly"},{"w":"āho","s":"sandehe, praśne ca","e":"particle of doubt; second part of a double interrogation, translatable as “or” (see āho svid for example)."},{"w":"āho svid","s":"praśne, sandehe ca","e":"second part of a double interrogation, translatable as “or” e.g kim īśvarānapekṣikam āho svid īśvarāpekṣam (“Is it independent of God or dependent on God?”); particle of doubt"},{"w":"i              khede, kope ca","s":"","e":"interjection of lamentation or anger"},{"w":"itas","s":"tataḥ, atra","e":"from this; here"},{"w":"itas tataḥ","s":"atra tatra","e":"here and there"},{"w":"itaredyus iti","s":"anya-dine idam-arthe, śeṣe, ata eva","e":"on another day this (quotation); thus ends; therefore, thus"},{"w":"itiha","s":"paramparāyām","e":"according to tradition"},{"w":"ittham","s":"anena prakāreṇa","e":"thus, in this way"},{"w":"idānīm","s":"adhunā","e":"now"},{"w":"iva","s":"sadṛśārthe, vākyālaṅkāre ca","e":"as if, like; ornamentation of a sentence"},{"w":"is","s":"khede, vismaye ca","e":"interjection of lamentation or wonder"},{"w":"iha","s":"atra","e":"in this, here"},{"w":"īṣat","s":"sv-alpe","e":"little, slightly"},{"w":"u            vitarke, pāda-pūraṇe ca","s":"interjection of conjecture; used for filling out a line of verse","e":""},{"w":"uccakais","s":"ucce, adhike ca","e":"high, loud; more"},{"w":"uccais","s":"ucce, adhike ca","e":"high, above, loud; more"},{"w":"uta","s":"saṁśaye, samuccaye ca","e":"particle of doubt; or"},{"w":"utāho","s":"praśne, vikalpe ca","e":"second part of a double interrogation, translatable as “or” e.g kaccit tvam asi mānuṣī utāho surāṅganā (“Are you a mortal woman or a demigoddess?); or"},{"w":"utāho svid","s":"praśne, vikalpe ca","e":"second part of a double interrogation, translatable as “or” (see utāho for example) ; or"},{"w":"uttaratas","s":"uttare","e":"to the north, on the north side"},{"w":"uttarāt","s":"uttare","e":"to the north, on the north side"},{"w":"uttareṇa","s":"uttare","e":"to the north, on the north side"},{"w":"uttaredyus","s":"para-dine","e":"tomorrow"},{"w":"udak","s":"uttarasyāṁ diśi","e":"in the northern direction"},{"w":"upajoṣam","s":"ānande, santoṣe ca","e":"blissfully, satisfactiroly"},{"w":"upayoṣam","s":"ānande, santoṣe ca","e":"blissfully, satisfactiroly"},{"w":"upari","s":"ucca-sthāne","e":"above, upon"},{"w":"upāṁśu","s":"nirjane","e":"secretly"},{"w":"ubhayatas","s":"ubhayena prakāreṇa","e":"in both ways"},{"w":"ubhayedyus","s":"ubhaya-dine","e":"on both days"},{"w":"um","s":"krodhe, pratijñāyāṁ ca","e":"interjection of anger; particle of assent"},{"w":"urarī","s":"svī-kāre","e":"particle of acceptance"},{"w":"urī","s":"svī-kāre","e":"particle of acceptance"},{"w":"ururi","s":"svī-kāre","e":"particle of acceptance"},{"w":"uṣā","s":"prātaḥ","e":"morning"},{"w":"ū            duḥkhe","s":"particle of misery","e":""},{"w":"ūm","s":"garve, krodhe ca","e":"particle of doubt or option"},{"w":"ūrarī","s":"svī-kāre","e":"particle of acceptance"},{"w":"ūrī","s":"svī-kāre","e":"particle of acceptance"},{"w":"ūruri","s":"svī-kāre","e":"particle of acceptance"},{"w":"ūrdhvam","s":"upari","e":"upwards, above, upon"},{"w":"ūṣā","s":"prātaḥ","e":"morning"},{"w":"ṛte","s":"vinā","e":"wihout, except"},{"w":"e            smaraṇe, sambodhane ca","s":"particle of remembrance; vocative","e":""},{"w":"ekatra","s":"eka-sthāne, saha-yogena","e":"in one place; all together"},{"w":"ekadā","s":"ekasmin samaye","e":"once"},{"w":"ekaikaśam","s":"eka-krameṇa","e":"one by one"},{"w":"etarhi","s":"idānīm, ataḥ kāraṇāt","e":"now, for this reason"},{"w":"eva","s":"avadhāraṇe","e":"particle of restriction which is used for emphasis, sometimes translatable as “only”"},{"w":"evam","s":"anena prakāreṇa, sammatau ca","e":"thus, so, in this way; yes"},{"w":"ai","s":"smaraṇe, sambodhane","e":"particle of remembrance; vocative"},{"w":"aiṣamas","s":"asmin vatsare","e":"in this year"},{"w":"o            sambodhane, smaraṇe ca om praṇave, svīkāre ca","s":"vocative; particle of remembrance oṁkāra; yes","e":""},{"w":"au","s":"sambodhane","e":"vocative"},{"w":"kaccid","s":"praśne, icchā-prakāśe ca","e":"a yes / no question marker translatable as “whether” in the word for word but as a question mark in the translation e.g kaccit te anāmayaṁ tāta (“Are you possessed of good health, my dear brother?”); particle revealing one’s desire, translatable as “I hope”"},{"w":"kati","s":"kiyati","e":"how many?"},{"w":"katham","s":"kena prakāreṇa","e":"how, in which way? why?"},{"w":"kadā","s":"kasmin samaye","e":"at which time? when?"},{"w":"kadācana","s":"kasmiṁścit samaye","e":"sometimes"},{"w":"kadācid","s":"kasmiṁścit samaye","e":"sometimes"},{"w":"karhi","s":"kadā","e":"sometimes"},{"w":"karhicid","s":"kasmiṁścit samaye","e":"sometimes"},{"w":"kāmam","s":"yatheṣṭam, paryāptam","e":"at will, freely; enough"},{"w":"kiṁ punaḥ","s":"vaktum adhikaṁ kim","e":"what more is there to say?"},{"w":"kiṁ vā","s":"atha vā","e":"or else"},{"w":"kiṁ svit","s":"sambhāvanāyām, vitarke ca","e":"possibly; perhaps"},{"w":"kiṁ ca","s":"api ca","e":"furthermore, moreover"},{"w":"kiñcana","s":"kiñcit","e":"little; something;"},{"w":"kiñcid","s":"sv-alpe, kiyad-aṁśe ca","e":"little; something;"},{"w":"kintu","s":"parantu","e":"but"},{"w":"kiṁ nu","s":"saṁśaye","e":"expression of doubt, translatable as “whether”"},{"w":"kim","s":"kutsitārthe, praśne, vitarke ca","e":"bad e.g kiṁ-rājā (“a bad king”); a yes / no question marker translatable as “whether” in the word for word but as a question mark in the translation e.g kim svapna etat (“Is this a dream?”), sometimes kim also means kim artham (“why?”); perhaps"},{"w":"kim iti","s":"kim artham","e":"why?"},{"w":"kim u","s":"sambhāvanāyām, vitarke ca","e":"possibly; perhaps"},{"w":"kim uta","s":"sambhāvanāyām, vitarke ca","e":"possibly; perhaps"},{"w":"kila","s":"niścitārthe, alīke, sambhāvanāyām, vārttāyāṁ ca","e":"certainly, indeed; falsely, pretendedly; possibly; reportedly"},{"w":"ku","s":"kutsite, pāpe, mande, amaṅgale ca","e":"contemptible, bad; sinful; slow, slightly; inauspicious"},{"w":"kutas","s":"kasmāt sthānāt, kiṁ nimittam","e":"from where?; why?"},{"w":"kutra","s":"kasmin sthāne, kasmin viṣaye","e":"where? on which topic?"},{"w":"kutracid","s":"kasmiṁścit sthāne","e":"somewhere"},{"w":"kṛtam","s":"vāraṇārthe","e":"enough of"},{"w":"kṛte","s":"nimittam","e":"for the sake of"},{"w":"keśākeśi","s":"keśeṣu keśeṣu ākramya yad yuddham","e":"hair to hair (head against head in battle)"},{"w":"kramaśas","s":"para-para-krameṇa","e":"sequentially"},{"w":"kva","s":"kutra","e":"where?"},{"w":"kvacana","s":"kutracit, kasmiṁścit samaye","e":"somewhere; at some time"},{"w":"khalu","s":"niścaye, vākyālaṅkāre ca","e":"certainly, indeed; ornamentation of a sentence"},{"w":"caturdhā","s":"catuḥ-prakāreṇa","e":"in four ways, fourfold"},{"w":"ciram","s":"cira-kālam, bahu-kālam (vyāpya)","e":"for a long time"},{"w":"cireṇa","s":"cira-kālam, bahu-kālam (vyāpya)","e":"for a long time"},{"w":"cirāya","s":"cira-kālam, bahu-kālam (vyāpya)","e":"for a long time"},{"w":"cira-rātrāya","s":"cira-kālam, bahu-kālam (vyāpya)","e":"for a long time"},{"w":"cirāt","s":"cira-kālam, bahu-kālam (vyāpya)","e":"for a long time"},{"w":"cirasya","s":"cira-kālam, bahu-kālam (vyāpya)","e":"for a long time"},{"w":"cire","s":"cira-kālam, bahu-kālam (vyāpya)","e":"for a long time"},{"w":"ced","s":"yadi","e":"if"},{"w":"jātu","s":"kadācit","e":"sometimes"},{"w":"joṣam","s":"tūṣṇīm, sukhe ca","e":"silently; happily"},{"w":"jhaṭiti","s":"śīghram","e":"quickly"},{"w":"tatas","s":"tasmād dhetoḥ, tad-anantaram","e":"therefore; after that, then"},{"w":"tatra","s":"tasmin sthāne","e":"there"},{"w":"tathā","s":"tena prakāreṇa","e":"thus, in that way"},{"w":"tathā hi","s":"dṛṣṭāntataḥ","e":"for example"},{"w":"tad","s":"tasmāt, tan-nimittam","e":"after that, then; therefore"},{"w":"tadā","s":"tasmin samaye","e":"then"},{"w":"tadānīm","s":"tasmin samaye","e":"then"},{"w":"tarhi","s":"tadā, tataḥ","e":"then; therefore"},{"w":"tāvat","s":"sākalye, vākyālaṅkāre, tat-parimite ca","e":"(i) totatily e.g yāvat dattam, tāvat bhuktam (“all that was given was eaten”) (ii) ornamentation of a sentence e.g itas tāvad āgamyatām (“first come here”), gaccha tāvat (“just go”), gatā tāvat (“she is indeed gone”), kas tāvad bhrama (“what is a bhrama, actually?”), saṁjñā tāvad dvi-vidhā, pūrvā avarā ca (“Saṁjñā is actually of two kinds: pūrvā and avarā”) (iii) measurement e.g so much, so many, so far, so long e.g tāvac chobate mūrkho yāvat kiñcin na bhāṣate (“so long a fool shines as long as he says nothing”)"},{"w":"tiras","s":"aprakāśe, vakrārthe ca","e":"(i) (as a prefix) disappearance e.g tiro-bhāvaḥ (“disappearance”), tiras-kāraḥ (“concealment, disregard”). (ii) (as an adverb) indirectly, across"},{"w":"tiryak","s":"vakrārthe, pārśve ca","e":"indirectly, across; on the side"},{"w":"tu","s":"kintu, punaḥ","e":"but; also"},{"w":"tūṣṇīm","s":"maunini, sthire ca","e":"silent; fixed"},{"w":"tris","s":"vāra-trayam","e":"three times, thrice"},{"w":"tredhā","s":"tri-prakāreṇa","e":"in three ways, threefold"},{"w":"traidham","s":"tri-prakāreṇa","e":"in three ways, threefold"},{"w":"dakṣiṇatas","s":"dakṣiṇāsyāṁ diśi","e":"to the south, on the south side"},{"w":"dakṣiṇāt","s":"dakṣiṇāsyāṁ diśi","e":"to the south, on the south side"},{"w":"dakṣiṇena","s":"dakṣiṇāsyāṁ diśi","e":"to the south, on the south side"},{"w":"daṇḍādaṇḍi","s":"daṇḍena daṇḍenākramya yad yuddham","e":"club against club (in battle)"},{"w":"divā","s":"dine","e":"during the day"},{"w":"diṣṭyā","s":"bhāgyena","e":"by good fortune"},{"w":"duṣṭhu","s":"ku, nindite","e":"same as ku; badly"},